Example 2: 10 -> 20 -> 30 -> 40 -> 50  (Odd length, Not Palindrome ✗)

--------------------------------- STEP 1: FIND MIDDLE ---------------------------------

Initial: slow=10, fast=10

Iteration 1:
  fast.next (20) != null ✓
  fast.next.next (30) != null ✓
  slow = 20, fast = 30

Iteration 2:
  fast.next (40) != null ✓
  fast.next.next (50) != null ✓
  slow = 30, fast = 50

Iteration 3:
  fast.next = null ✗
  Exit loop

Middle: slow = 30 (exact middle for odd length)

List: 10 -> 20 -> 30 -> 40 -> 50
                   ↑
                 slow


--------------------------------- STEP 2: REVERSE SECOND HALF ---------------------------------

slow.next = 40
Reverse: 40 -> 50  →  50 -> 40

rvs = 50

Full List Now:
10 -> 20 -> 30 -> 40 <- 50
                   ↑    ↑
                 slow  rvs


--------------------------------- STEP 3: COMPARE ---------------------------------

cur = 10, rvs = 50

Iteration 1:
  cur.data (10) != rvs.data (50) ✗

Mismatch found → Return FALSE ✗


--------------------------------- VISUAL ---------------------------------

Original:     10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50
              ↑            ↑
            head         slow

After Reverse:
First Half:   10 → 20 → 30
Second Half:  50 ← 40  (reversed)
              ↑
            rvs

Compare:      10 ≠ 50  ✗ (Fail immediately)


--------------------------------- EDGE CASE: SINGLE NODE ---------------------------------

Input: 5 -> null

Step 1: slow=5, fast=5
  fast.next = null → Exit immediately

Step 2: rvs = reverse(slow.next) = reverse(null) = null

Step 3: while(rvs != null) → Loop doesn't run

Return TRUE ✓ (Single node is always palindrome)


