--------------------------------- KEY POINTS ---------------------------------

✓ Slow/fast pointers find middle in O(n/2) time
✓ Reverse only second half (saves space)
✓ Compare first half with reversed second half
✓ Only traverse reversed half (shorter comparison)
✓ Handles both even and odd lengths correctly
✓ Single node returns true automatically

Time: O(n)  |  Space: O(1)  [Only pointers, no extra data structure]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Palindrome Linked List
Given the head of a singly linked list, check if it reads the same forward and backward.

Example 1:
Input: 1 → 2 → 1 → 1 → 2 → 1
Output: true
Explanation: Reads same forward and backward.

Example 2:
Input: 10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50
Output: false
Explanation: 10→20→30→40→50 ≠ 50→40→30→20→10.

Constraints:
- 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10⁵
- 0 ≤ node->data ≤ 10³

Your Approach: Slow/Fast Pointers + Reverse
1. Find middle using slow/fast pointers (O(n/2))
2. Reverse second half in-place (O(n/2))
3. Compare first half with reversed second half (O(n/2))
4. Return false on mismatch, true if all match

Time: O(n) | Space: O(1) ✓ Optimal
